Description: Skip building the unshipped test and example executables
 This package ships ONLY the private-dir libfprint-2 runtime library for the
 egismoc driver. Upstream's meson builds the test and example programs
 unconditionally (no option gates subdir('tests')/subdir('examples')), which
 needlessly compiles and LTO-links a stack of executables we never install —
 wasting build time/memory on the Launchpad builders. Drop those subdirs so the
 build graph contains only the library we ship.
 .
 Debian-packaging change only; NOT part of the upstream (MR 547) patch series.
Author: Philip Walsh <packages@drphilth.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-07-07
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -367,9 +367,8 @@
 endif
 
 subdir('data')
-subdir('tests')
-
-subdir('examples')
+# Debian packaging (honor-fmbp-libfprint-sdcp): ship ONLY the egismoc runtime
+# library; skip building the unshipped test/example executables.
 
